8 cores shared with the other projects' seats (the drafter read load averages 4.96 3.35 3.65 at 03:27 AEDT, up 11 days). **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent reads: say so), recorded beside the result; at or over, poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile (writing the test, the swap programs). Heavy = `docker build`, any database-container run, the `packages/db` group, any vitest over more than one file, the unit chain. **One heavy job of yours at a time**, behind `.tools/b778/lock`. Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). Never leave a background job running when you finish. NO artificial load. Remove ONLY your own `pc-b778-*` containers, networks and the anonymous postgres volumes your runs created, by exact name, after the log is saved.

